{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792169978,"nonce":"xUfZQ+Kv098og9znPoi5y8LIcf8=","title":"A multi-word button label wraps even when its flex row has room","message":"Reported from ChimpMonk's editor: an alert-dialog footer\n`\u003cdialog-footer\u003e\u003cbutton variant={Outline}\u003eDon't save\u003c/button\u003e\u003cdialog-close\u003eCancel\u003c/dialog-close\u003e\u003cbutton\u003eSave\u003c/button\u003e\u003c/dialog-footer\u003e`.\nThe footer is 318px wide with 76px free on the left\n(justify-content: flex-end), yet the first button's text lays out as\n57x34 (two lines) inside a 91x52 button. The same label as the LAST\nbutton in a footer (\"Move to Trash\") stays on one line. Not focus,\nnot the apostrophe (both checked). Workaround used: a one-word label\n(\"Discard\").\n\nSmells like something about NOT being the last flex child (or being\nfollowed by other buttons) affects this button's own text-wrap\nmeasurement, independent of actual available width.","files":null}]}